Phase 1: MDX Blog & Day 1 Public Vision (Day 1 Priority)
Implement an MDX-powered interactive engineering blog within the LaunchPilot platform on Day 1 to establish full public transparency, publish interactive build logs, and outline expected outcomes before module development begins.
Day 1 Content Rollout Plan
* Initial Post 1 (Day 1): Core Vision, Mission Statement, and the Paradigm Shift ("Why Code Execution Speed Is No Longer the Bottleneck").
* Initial Post 2 (Day 1/2): Detailed Phased Execution Roadmap with estimated target completion dates.
* Initial Post 3 (Day 3): The Expected Business & Technical Results (target 50 solo devs on SaaS Pass, <50ms edge latencies, Acquire.com exit packaging target).
Technical MDX Stack (Day 1 Setup)
* Framework & Infrastructure: MDX integrated into Next.js / Cloudflare Pages to enable immediate blogging on Day 1.
* Component Integration: Setup dynamic interactive widgets inside markdown (e.g., <WtpCalculator />, <RoadmapTimeline />, <TelemetryChart />).
* Git Pipeline & Frontmatter: File-based blogging workflow (content/posts/*.mdx) with frontmatter parsing (title, date, phase tag, target outcomes, author).
OpenSpec & Deliverables Breakdown
* OpenSpec Deliverables: openspec/module-f-mdx-blog.md: Specification for MDX component safety boundaries, frontmatter attributes, interactive widget props (<WtpCalculator />, <RoadmapTimeline />), dynamic widget rendering on serverless edge, and RSS/Atom feed generators.
* Google AI Studio Task: Draft MDX post templates, prompts for converting commit history into public build logs, and component contracts.
* OpenHands Execution: Implement MDX compiler middleware, build interactive React UI components (<WtpCalculator />, <RoadmapTimeline />), and deploy static asset generation on Cloudflare Pages.
